{title: 388 - Don't Forget the Sabbath}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb/F]Don't forget the Sabbath, The Lord our [F]God hath [F7]blest,
[F7]Of all [Bb]the week the brightest, Of all the week [F]the best;
[F]It brings repose from labor, It tells [F7]of joy divine,
[Bb]Its beams of [F/A]light descending, [Bb]With heav'nly beauty shine.
[Bb]Welcome, welcome, ever [F]welcome, Blessèd [Bb/F]Sabbath day.
[Bb]Welcome, [F7/A]welcome, ever [Bb]welcome, Blessèd [Eb/Bb]Sabbath [F]day.

Refrain:
[F]Welcome, [Eb/Bb]welcome, [Bb]ever welcome,
[Bb]Blessed Sabbath day,
[Bb]Welcome, [Eb/Bb]welcome, ever [F]welcome,
[F]Blessed Sabbath [Bb/F]day.

Verse 2:
[Bb/F]Keep the Sabbath holy,
[F7]And [Bb]worship Him today,
[F7]Who [Bb]said to His disciples,
[F]"I am the living [F7/C]way;"
[Bb]And if [F/A]we [Bb]meekly follow
[Bb]Our Savior [F]here below,
[Bb]He'll give us [F]of the [Bb/F]fountain
[Bb]Whose [F7/A]streams eternal [Eb/Bb]flow.

Verse 3:
[Bb/F]Day of sacred pleasure!
[F7]Its [Bb]golden hours we'll [F]spend
[F7]In [Bb]thankful hymns to Jesus,
[F]The children's dearest [F7/C]Friend;
[Bb]O gentle loving, Savior,
[Bb]How good and [F]kind Thou [Bb/F]art,
[Bb]How precious [F]is Thy [Bb/F]promise
[Bb]To dwell [F7/A]in [Bb]every heart!
